## 1. Purpose and License Model

The Amaru Community License makes the Amaru source code available for inspection, learning, modification, self-hosting, and community collaboration.

The license permits personal use and internal commercial use while reserving commercial distribution, resale, commercial sublicensing, and the provision of the Software as a commercial hosted service to LUDERS TECNOLOGIA LTDA, subject to the rights of third-party copyright holders and applicable law.

This is a source-available, Fair-Code license. It is not an OSI-approved Open Source license, and no claim of OSI approval is made.

## 2. Definitions

**"Software"** means the source code, object code, documentation, and associated materials distributed under this license by or with authorization from the Rights Holder.

**"Rights Holder"** means LUDERS TECNOLOGIA LTDA, CNPJ 63.631.031/0001-60, acting only within the scope of rights it owns or is authorized to license.

**"Modification"** means any change, extension, adaptation, or derivative work based on the Software.

**"Internal Use"** means use of the Software by an individual or organization for its own activities, including commercial business operations, provided that the Software is not itself commercially distributed, resold, sublicensed, or offered as a Hosted Service to third parties in violation of this license.

**"Hosted Service"** means a product or service through which a third party can access, interact with, or use material functionality of the Software over a network, including a SaaS platform, managed runtime, hosted agent execution platform, or remotely operated service.

A service is not excluded from this definition merely because it is based on a fork, Modification, renamed product, modified user interface, or additional components.

A business does not violate the Hosted Service restriction merely by using the Software internally to conduct its own business, develop its own products, or support its own employees, provided it does not make the Software's material functionality available to third parties as a service.

**"Commercial Distribution"** means selling, reselling, commercially licensing, sublicensing, or otherwise supplying the Software or a Modification to third parties as a commercial offering.

**"Contribution"** means code, documentation, designs, or other material intentionally submitted by a contributor for inclusion in, or integration with, the Software.

**"Contributor License Agreement" or "CLA"** means a separate written agreement accepted by a contributor and the Rights Holder that establishes the rights granted over Contributions.

