## 5. Commercial Distribution and Hosted Services

Unless expressly authorized by a separate written commercial license granted by the Rights Holder, you may not:

- Sell or resell the Software or a Modification.
- Grant commercial sublicenses to the Software or a Modification.
- Offer the Software or a Modification as a commercial Hosted Service.
- Operate a SaaS, managed service, or remotely accessible execution platform that provides third parties with material functionality of the Software.
- Commercially distribute a product that incorporates the Software or a Modification.
- Circumvent these restrictions by forking, renaming, rebranding, wrapping, or modifying the Software.

These restrictions apply regardless of whether the Software or a fork is offered under the Amaru name.

They do not prohibit Internal Use or self-hosting for personal use or Internal Use. They also do not prohibit the use of the Software as an internal engineering tool to build or operate unrelated commercial products, provided that the Software itself is not supplied to third parties in a manner prohibited by this license.

A separate written commercial license is required for activities reserved under this section.

