## 7. Contributions and Contributor License Agreement

### 7.1 Acceptance of Contributions

External Contributions will be accepted for integration into the official Amaru project only after the contributor has executed a Contributor License Agreement (CLA) approved by the Rights Holder.

The project should link to the applicable CLA from its contribution guidelines and contribution workflow.

Submitting a pull request, opening an issue, or otherwise communicating with the project does not, by itself, transfer copyright ownership or grant the Rights Holder commercial licensing rights.

Contributions must not be merged as accepted project Contributions until the applicable CLA has been recorded as executed, unless the Rights Holder has established a documented alternative agreement that grants equivalent rights.

### 7.2 Rights Granted by the CLA

The CLA must expressly grant the Rights Holder a worldwide, perpetual, irrevocable, non-exclusive, royalty-free license, with the right to sublicense and transfer the licensed rights, to:

- Use, reproduce, modify, adapt, and create derivative works from the Contribution.
- Incorporate the Contribution into the Software and related products.
- Distribute, publicly display, perform, and make the Contribution available.
- Commercially exploit the Contribution.
- Include the Contribution in proprietary or commercially licensed versions of the Software.
- License and sublicense the Contribution under terms different from this community license, including commercial terms.

The CLA must also establish the contributor's authority to grant these rights and address applicable third-party rights.

### 7.3 Ownership of Contributions

Unless a separate written agreement expressly provides otherwise, contributors retain ownership of the copyright in their Contributions to the extent that they own those rights.

The CLA grants the Rights Holder the rights specified in that agreement but does not automatically transfer ownership of a Contribution.

Contributors must not submit material they do not have the legal authority to license under the applicable CLA.

### 7.4 Contributions Without a CLA

Contributions for which the required rights have not been established must not be merged into the official project as accepted Contributions.

The project may request a signed CLA, an alternative written agreement granting equivalent rights, or a replacement implementation created by authorized contributors.

